--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/drivers/radv/bc250-mesh.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+BC-250 mesh shader compatibility
+================================
+
+GFX1013 remains a native GFX10 device for ordinary rendering. RADV enables a
+mesh-only compatibility policy by default on this ASIC: true mesh shader
+stages are compiled with GFX10.3 semantics, while vertex, tessellation,
+geometry, fragment, compute, surfaces, synchronization, and VRS retain the
+native device level. Task shaders are not exposed because RADV's native task
+path requires the disabled ACE/compute-only queue.
+
+Set ``RADV_BC250_MESH=0`` to disable the experimental mesh policy. The value
+is captured when the physical device is created and does not change afterward.
+Set ``RADV_BC250_MESH_LOG=1`` to print the selected policy.
+
+The compatibility mode is included in RADV's device cache key, so native GFX10
+and mesh-compatible shader binaries cannot collide. The mode does not modify
+VRS feature reporting or state programming.
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
